  <dashboards>
    <dashboard enable-sort-zone-taborder='true' name='Dashboard 1'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Breast Cancer Treatment Cost &amp; Pathway Analysis</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
      </layout-options>
      <style />
      <size sizing-mode='automatic' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='4' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='98020' id='21' param='horz' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98698' x='651' y='990'>
            <zone h='98020' id='18' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98698' x='651' y='990'>
              <zone h='4827' id='19' type-v2='title' w='98698' x='651' y='990'>
                <zone-style>
                  <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                  <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                  <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                  <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                </zone-style>
              </zone>
              <zone h='6931' id='22' type-v2='text' w='98698' x='651' y='5817'>
                <formatted-text>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>This analysis asks: does treatment cost and pathway differ meaningfully for breast cancer patients, and does treatment intensity predict cost? The data confirms the first: this cohort averages nearly double the healthcare cost of the general population. The second answer is more surprising: patients on targeted hormone therapy without chemotherapy show the highest average cost, not the patients receiving full chemo regimens, a result explained by the high per-dose cost of modern targeted biologic drugs.</run>
                </formatted-text>
                <zone-style>
                  <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                  <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                  <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                  <format attr='margin' value='4' />
